//! The database models: one SeaORM entity per table (`tasks::Entity`, `tasks::Column`, `tasks::ActiveModel`),
//! with the row itself, `tasks::Model`, re-exported under its singular name (`Task`). The files are generated by
//! `mise run gen:models` (`sea-orm-cli generate entity`) and then edited: dates are our jiff
//! [`DateTime`](crate::time::DateTime), enum columns are the `ActiveEnum`s in `enums`, and a few rows carry
//! `Serialize`/`ToSchema` because the API returns them as they are. Regenerating overwrites the files, so run it
//! on a clean tree and review `git diff` (this file is edited by hand too: the `enums` module and the aliases).
//!
//! - Every date-time is a [`DateTime`](crate::time::DateTime): a `jiff::civil::DateTime` meaning UTC (see
//!   `crate::time`), stored as text; task dates are a day at midnight UTC.
//! - Users' things are soft deleted (`deleted_at`); who deleted them is in the `AuditLog`.
//! - Ordering uses integer positions spaced 20 apart (see `crate::ordering`).
//! - Relations are foreign keys (SQLite enforces them; the connections turn `foreign_keys` on), so a row cannot
//!   point at nothing, and nothing that has children is ever hard deleted.

